# Slice 337 (Codex, review of 331, item 2: the path in field 0 of an ordinary Frame, normalized when the graph is built):
# a Frame written on a path head, `owner\field: value`, is the write of that field, at the root and in a body, as
# `owner\field := value` is -- the head is resolved first, the one value is computed after it, and a value may read the
# body's own names (d, x). Before, the head stayed one word: the root defined a new place named `Box\hits`, a body
# answered 3.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and the call main().
# The two root writes and v1 stay at the root as paths into the data of main and run before main(); bump and twice are
# written in the code of main and write Box by its name there.
sub: main () (
    Box:
        int: hits 0
        Inner(int: v 1)
    int: t 0
)
    sub: bump (int: d 1)
        Box\hits := Box\hits + d
    bump(10)
    bump()
    fn: twice (int: x) int
        Box\Inner\v := x * 2
        return: Box\Inner\v
    t := twice(21)
main\data\Box\hits := 5
main\data\Box\Inner\v := main\data\Box\hits + 2
int: v1 main\data\Box\Inner\v
main()
int: t main\data\t
int: h main\data\Box\hits
int: v2 main\data\Box\Inner\v
